diff --git a/docs/spec/p25-codeplug.md b/docs/spec/p25-codeplug.md
index 985877b..9a2824d 100644
--- a/docs/spec/p25-codeplug.md
+++ b/docs/spec/p25-codeplug.md
@@ -82,7 +82,12 @@ A P25 channel the radio saves (a VFO in P25 stored as a channel, a mode changed
 system, transmit allowed from the channel and a full parameter block: the RX and TX NAC, and the squelch selective
 where the settings name a talk group to hear, else normal. Its contact is the stored contact of the talk target, if
 any (else none: talk group 1). Talkaround on sets the direct-mode bit; automatic and off leave it clear (automatic, 2.2).
-A session unit ID is not stored. Editing a channel that is P25 already rewrites its record and lets the tag follow,
+A session unit ID is not stored. On the radio, open Channels, choose the conventional channel, choose
+**Talkgroup / unit**, and pick a stored contact. The row shows the numeric destination: TG for a group, ID for a unit.
+Hold OK to save. In the VFO or on a conventional channel, Quick menu key 8 **TG** lets you type a group from 1 to
+65535. The VFO setting is for the current session. On a memory channel it is temporary until you hold **OK** on Home to save,
+which requires the talkgroup to be a stored contact.
+Editing a channel that is P25 already rewrites its record and lets the tag follow,
 the block kept byte for byte; a copy at another number takes the source's tag ([channel-modes.md](channel-modes.md)
 2.4). When the channel editor changed the NAC ([ui.md](ui.md) 2.1), the record is written as the safe stand-in and
 the tag follows it, then the edited NACs and the squelch as read are written over the front of its block
